  <!-- What's new after an update -->
  <string name="whats_new_title">What\'s new in 2.5.2</string>
  <string name="whats_new_body">NEW IN 2.5.2\n• Mixed-language text switches voice the way eSpeak does: Hindi inside English text is read by your Hindi natural voice. Choose a natural voice for both languages; on phones with less memory the main voice reads everything.\n• Central Kurdish reads words that start with two consonants correctly, like نڤێژ, and uses the Kurdish r sounds.\n• Malayalam words ending in a chillu letter and Persian words with a joiner are read correctly again.\n• Combined emoji, like a family, are named as one again.\n• Very long text without punctuation no longer breaks an emoji in two.\n• Give feedback from About: join the adev ally group on WhatsApp.\n\nFIXED IN 2.5.1\n• The user dictionary opens again, and rules can be edited and deleted.\n• Natural voices no longer crash speech, including when moving quickly through items.\n• A natural voice that keeps failing on your phone switches to eSpeak instead of stopping speech.\n• Natural voices are off until you turn them on, and nothing about them runs while off.\n• The app no longer uses the internet at start-up; only voice downloads do.\n• Download suggestions match what your phone can play without pauses.\n• Dictionary export keeps every part of each rule and matches NVDA\'s format.\n• Speech keeps working even if a setting is damaged.\n• Activity logs and backups no longer include your reading history.\n• Clearer error messages, and no crash on devices without a file picker.\n\nNATURAL VOICES\n• Download human-sounding voices and choose, language by language, whether eSpeak or a natural voice speaks. They follow this app\'s pronunciation rules and your dictionary. Turn them on in Natural voices; until then everything is plain eSpeak.\n• Standard and Enhanced quality, with a suggestion for your phone.\n• Community voices for Tamil and Sinhala.\n• Long texts play smoothly, voices load in about a second and use little memory.\n• Hindi and Urdu sentences end with a natural tone.\n\nNEW FEATURES\n• Settings search from the top bar.\n• Voice profiles: save and share your variant, rate, pitch and punctuation as a file.\n• Favorite voices stay at the top of the voice list.\n• Sleep timer, in Locks.\n• Reading history (opt-in), in Tools.\n• Touch and hold a language to hear a sample.\n\nVOICES AND LANGUAGES\n• Better pronunciation for Assamese, Gujarati, Nepali, Punjabi, Konkani and Sinhala.\n• Indian English sounds closer to real Indian English.\n• Lakh and crore reading can be used with every voice, and Hinglish, abbreviations and money reading work with more voices.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n• TalkBack moves to the first setting when a page opens, and sliders announce their value once.\n• TalkBack knows these voices work offline.\n\nLOOK AND STABILITY\n• A refreshed, modern design.\n• Faster start-up and more reliable voice setup.</string>

